    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "df3fd718a1686aea",
      "text": "Claude review, I1: Should the new :code method of dreyeck/verified-example preserve the prior Inspector rendering of unmarked Code story items, their Inspector object reference included?"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "3c4579ae4f9f9b52",
      "text": "Claude review, context, observed by reading: the new method is defined at [https://github.com/RalfBarkow/hyperdoc/blob/9b57bd4bb87d92fbf3061b91a42a6f539e18cdb1/dreyeck/src/verified-example.lisp#L160-L166 verified-example.lisp lines 160-166]; for Code items it takes the place of the fallback method at [https://github.com/RalfBarkow/hyperdoc/blob/9b57bd4bb87d92fbf3061b91a42a6f539e18cdb1/hyperbook-fedwiki/story-items.lisp#L109-L115 story-items.lisp lines 109-115]."
    },
    {
      "type": "pagefold",
      "id": "0d0714860cd6261b",
      "text": "claim"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "f7be8ac42a455495",
      "text": "Claude review, Position A: [[Preserve the Prior Code Rendering]]"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "a4a709dee2b9f04c",
      "text": "Claude review, Position B: [[Passive Code Rendering May Be Intended]]"
    },
    {
      "type": "pagefold",
      "id": "333540752a0bed22",
      "text": "~"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "e3a68197ef358df2",
      "text": "Claude review, not executed: the probe P1 would render one unmarked Code item before and after loading dreyeck/verified-example, in a fresh process, and compare the HTML and the Inspector references. Until it runs, the difference between the two renderings is derived from reading only. Even once it has run, whether the difference is a defect stays this question."
    },
